      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "ASK",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — the command typed",
      "narration_text": "In the terminal: ask Claude to write a PSI function using equal-width bucketing on the training distribution. Then generate a training set from a standard normal and test it against three scenarios: no shift, moderate shift at mean point-five, and a major shift at mean one-point-five with increased variance. Print PSI for each and flag anything above point-two.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "claude \"Write psi(expected, actual, buckets=10)\ncomputing Population Stability Index.\nPSI = sum((actual_pct - expected_pct) * ln(actual_pct / expected_pct))\nGenerate:\n  training: N(0,1) 5000 samples\n  test: no-shift N(0,1), moderate N(0.5,1), major N(1.5,1.2)\nPrint PSI for each. Flag >0.2 as major drift.\"",
            "topic": "COMPUTATIONAL SKEPTICISM — DISTRIBUTION SHIFT (PSI)",
            "segment": "DISTRIBUTION SHIFT DETECTOR",
            "greeting": "",
            "runningText": "generating PSI distribution monitor…",
            "output": [],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Fable 5",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 19.46,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T17:06:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "CODE",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — read the code before running",
      "narration_text": "Read the PSI formula. PSI equals the sum over all buckets of actual percent minus expected percent, times the log of actual percent over expected percent. It is a symmetrized KL divergence. The log term penalizes large ratio changes; the difference term penalizes large absolute shifts. Below point-one: stable. Point-one to point-two: monitor. Above point-two: retrain.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "psi_monitor.py",
            "code": "# psi_monitor.py  —  Claude Code output\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef psi(expected, actual, buckets=10):\n    \"\"\"Population Stability Index — symmetric KL divergence.\"\"\"\n    # Build bucket edges from TRAINING (expected) distribution\n    lo, hi = expected.min(), expected.max()\n    edges = np.linspace(lo, hi, buckets + 1)\n    \n    e_counts, _ = np.histogram(expected, bins=edges)\n    a_counts, _ = np.histogram(actual,   bins=edges)\n    \n    # Percentages (add epsilon to avoid log(0))\n    e_pct = (e_counts + 1e-6) / len(expected)\n    a_pct = (a_counts + 1e-6) / len(actual)\n    \n    psi_val = np.sum((a_pct - e_pct) * np.log(a_pct / e_pct))\n    return psi_val\n\n# Thresholds: <0.1 stable  |  0.1-0.2 monitor  |  >0.2 RETRAIN",
            "sparkLine": "DISTRIBUTION SHIFT DETECTOR"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 21.31,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T17:06:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "OUTPUT — run",
      "role_note": "Manim animation: B04_PSIBars",
      "narration_text": "Run it. Three horizontal bars. No shift: PSI point-zero-zero-one, almost invisible — the training and test distributions are identical. Moderate shift: PSI point-zero-eight, a medium bar, still in the monitoring zone. Major drift: PSI point-three-zero, a long crimson bar crossing the point-two threshold line. Retrain alert. The model cannot see this — it has no input monitor. You built one.",
      "visual_intent": "Manim B04_PSIBars: three horizontal bars growing from left — no-shift green (tiny), moderate gold (medium), major-drift crimson (long) crossing PSI=0.20 threshold dashed line with RETRAIN ALERT annotation",
